<title>UK: Pentland sells Miller Ent for 10.8 mln stg.</title>
<headline>Pentland sells Miller Ent for 10.8 mln stg.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Britain's Pentland Group Plc said on Wednesday it sold its greetings card business, Miller Enterprises Ltd, to a management buy-out team for 10.8 million stg.</p>
<p>Pentland said out of the consideration, 6.2 million stg related to the equity of the business, while 4.6 million concerned the repayment of inter-company indebtedness.</p>
<p>The net assets of Miller stood at 5.1 million stg as on December 31, 1995.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
